1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,000
Four movements. One small robot.
A virtual model explains the project. Actual hardware still needs testing.

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:16,000
Turn left. Turn right.
Moving the base rotates the whole arm around its vertical axis.

3
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:24,000
Raise the arm. Lower the arm.
The shoulder lifts the links and everything they carry.

4
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:32,000
Reach out. Fold back.
Changing the elbow angle changes the reach of the gripper.

5
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:40,000
Open. Close. Hold an object.
Close gently around an object. Grip strength depends on the real mechanism.

6
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:48,000
You move the stick. The Uno responds.
Servos use a separate rated supply. Connect supply ground to Uno ground.

7
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:56,000
Reach. Grip. Lift. Turn. Place.
The scripted motion here is a simulation, not an autonomous hardware feature.

8
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:04,000
Wire. Calibrate. Test. Then extend.
Camera → Python → USB → Uno is a planned upgrade, not implemented yet.
